You look, but it doesn't hold your interest.	你看了看，卻提不起興致。
This is no time for idle chatter.	此刻不是閒聊的時候。
I am not in the mood for small talk.	我沒有心情閒話家常。
If I have something to say, I will say it.	我若有話要說，自會開口。
That is not the proper invocation.	那並非正確的咒語。
I would not advise that.	我不建議如此。
That is not wise.	此舉並不明智。
That would be most foolish.	此舉實屬愚昧。
Even a king should not throw money away frivolously.	即便貴為國王，也不該任意揮霍金錢。
You know what they say about a fool and his money.	俗話說得好：愚人與錢財，總是易散難聚。
I have nothing to tell you now.	我此刻無話可說。
Your purse is as empty as a fool's mind.	你的錢囊，空得如同愚人的腦袋。
Your purse is as empty as a maiden's womb.	你的錢囊，空得如同少女的腹中。
It is dark and dreary in your purse, rather like a miser's curse.	你的錢囊裡陰暗淒涼，恰似守財奴的詛咒。
Your purse is as empty as an abbot's heart.	你的錢囊，空得如同修道院長那顆冷淡的心。
Your purse holds naught. Which is a naughty state of affairs for a king.	你的錢囊分文不剩，這般寒酸光景，對一位國王來說實在不成體統。
Your purse is as empty as the devil's conscience. And that is very empty indeed.	你的錢囊，空得如同魔鬼的良心——那可是空得徹底。
There is nothing here to fight.	此處無物可戰。
A wise warrior knows when it is time to fight and when it is not.	智勇的戰士，懂得何時該戰、何時該忍。
Save your readiness for a time when danger is upon you.	留著你的戒備，待危險當前之時再用。
Three lives have I. Gentle enough to soothe the skin, Light enough to caress the sky, Hard enough to crack rocks.      What am I?	我有三種樣貌：溫柔時能撫平肌膚，輕盈時能拂過長空，堅硬時能裂開頑石。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「water」）
Lighter than what I am made of, More of me is hidden Than is seen.      What am I?	我比造就我的東西更輕盈，藏於水下的我，遠比露出水面的我更多。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「iceberg」）
When I am filled I can point the way, When I am empty Nothing moves me, I have two skins One without and one within.      What am I?	填滿之時，我能為你指路；空空之時，任誰也無法驅動我；我有兩層皮——一層在外，一層在內。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「gloves」）
If a man carried my burden He would break his back. I am not rich, But leave silver in my track.      What am I?	若讓一個人扛起我的重擔，他的脊背定會斷裂；我並不富有，行過之處卻總留下一道銀痕。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「snail」）
My life can be measured in hours, I serve by being devoured. Thin, I am quick Fat, I am slow Wind is my foe.      What am I?	我的一生以時辰計量，我在被吞噬中盡我職責；瘦時，我燃得快；胖時，我燃得慢；風，是我的天敵。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「candle」）
To unravel me You need a simple key, No key that was made By locksmith's hand, But a key that only I Will understand.      What am I?	要解開我，你需要一把鑰匙；那並非鎖匠打造的鑰匙，而是唯獨我才懂的那一把。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「riddle」）
Weight in my belly, Trees on my back, Nails in my ribs, Feet I do lack.      What am I?	腹中裝載重物，背上立著樹木，肋骨間釘著鐵釘，卻沒有一雙腳。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「ship」）
If you break me I do not stop working, If you touch me I may be snared, If you lose me Nothing will matter.      What am I?	縱使破碎，我仍不停跳動；輕觸於我，我便可能為之淪陷；失去了我，世間再無一物要緊。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「heart」）
I turn around once, What is out will not get in. I turn around again, What is in will not get out      What am I?	我轉動一次，門外之物便進不來；我再轉動一次，門內之物便出不去。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「key」）
I am only useful When I am full, Yet I am always Full of holes.      What am I?	唯有滿載之時，我才派得上用場，但我渾身上下，卻始終佈滿了孔洞。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「net」）
You can see nothing else When you look in my face, I will look you in the eye And I will never lie.      What am I?	望進我的臉龐，你便再看不見其他事物；我會直視你的雙眼，且從不欺瞞。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「mirror」）
I drive men mad For love of me, Easily beaten, Never free.      What am I?	世人為愛我而癡狂，我輕易便能被錘打成形，卻永遠不得自由。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「gold」）
Glittering points That downward thrust, Sparkling spears That never rust.      What am I?	閃爍的尖端向下垂刺，晶亮的長矛永不生鏽。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「icicle」）
When set loose I fly away, Never so cursed As when I go astray.      What am I?	一旦脫手，我便振翅飛去；一旦偏離了目標，便再沒有比那更該受詛咒的了。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「arrow」）
When young, I am sweet in the sun. When middle-aged, I make you gay. When old, I am valued more than ever.      What am I?	年輕之時，我在陽光下香甜可口；到了中年，我能令你歡欣暢懷；待到年邁，世人卻對我愈發珍視。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「wine」）
I am always hungry, I must always be fed, The finger I lick Will soon turn red.      What am I?	我永遠飢餓，總須被人餵養；被我舔過的手指，很快便會泛紅。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「fire」）
Each morning I appear To lie at your feet, All day I follow No matter how fast you run, Yet I nearly perish In the midday sun.      What am I?	每日清晨，我伏於你的腳邊現身；終日跟隨，任你跑得多快也甩不開我；然而正午豔陽下，我卻幾近消散。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「shadow」）
Bright as diamonds, Loud as thunder, Never still, A thing of wonder.      What am I?	亮如鑽石，響若雷鳴，從不靜止，是造化的奇景一樁。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「waterfall」）
You heard me before, Yet you hear me again, Then I die, 'Til you call me again.      What am I?	你曾聽過我的聲音，如今又再度聽見；隨後我便消逝，直到你再次呼喚我。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「echo」）
Lovely and round, I shine with pale light, grown in the darkness, A lady's delight.      What am I?	美麗而渾圓，我泛著蒼白微光，於幽暗中孕育而成，是淑女鍾愛的珍寶。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「pearl」）
Until I am measured I am not known, Yet how you miss me When I have flown.      What am I?	在被量度之前，無人識得我；然而一旦我飛逝而去，你才驚覺自己多麼想念我。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「time」）
All about, but cannot be seen, Can be captured, cannot be held, No throat, but can be heard.      What am I?	我無處不在，卻無形無跡；能被捕捉，卻無法握住；沒有喉嚨，卻能被聽見。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「wind」）
I am seen in the water If seen in the sky, I am in the rainbow, A jay's feather, And lapis lazuli.      What am I?	若我現於天際，也會映在水中；我存在於彩虹裡、松鴉的羽翼上，也存在於青金石中。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「blue」）
I go around in circles But always straight ahead, Never complain No matter where I am led.      What am I?	我不斷繞著圈子打轉，卻始終一路向前；無論被引往何方，我從不埋怨。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「wheel」）
At the sound of me, men may dream Or stamp their feet At the sound of me, women may laugh Or sometimes weep.      What am I?	聽見我的聲音，男子或陷入遐想，或隨之踏步；聽見我的聲音，女子或展顏而笑，或潸然落淚。      我是什麼？（請以英文作答：「music」）
Nay, that is not the answer. You had better guess again, sir.	不，那並非正確答案。爵士，你最好再猜一次。
The proper word Is yet unheard.	正確之語，尚未曾聞。
You shall not pass with that word, alas.	唉，那字尚不足以讓你通過。
The way shall not be open Until the proper word is spoken.	道路將不會開啟，直到正確之語出口。
Nothing	空無一物
She was the Goddess of Byblos.	她是比布魯斯的女神。
Among her other names were Astroarche, Attar-Samayin and Ishtar.	她的別名尚有 Astroarche、Attar-Samayin，以及伊絲塔。
The Israelites burned incense, offered wine and baked cakes in her honor.	以色列人焚香、獻酒、烤製糕餅，以示對她的尊崇。
She had a great shrine at Aphaca.	她在阿法卡建有一座宏偉的聖殿。
King Solomon built a sanctuary in her honor in Jerusalem.	所羅門王在耶路撒冷為她建造了一座聖所。
Her priestesses were famous for their skill in astrology.	她的女祭司以精通占星之術聞名。
She was earlier known as a Goddess in the country of Libya.	她起初是利比亞人所信奉的女神。
According to Greek legends, she was born from the forehead of Zeus.	依希臘傳說，她是從宙斯的額頭誕生的。
She was the patron of architects, sculptors, spinners and weavers.	她是建築師、雕刻家、紡織工與織工的守護神。
The element of brimstone was associated with her.	硫磺這項元素，與她有所關聯。
The name of her major temple means "virgin-house."	她主要神殿的名字，意為「處女之屋」。
She was renowned for her wisdom, which was often represented in the form of an owl sitting upon her shoulder.	她以智慧聞名於世，常以一隻棲於肩頭的貓頭鷹作為象徵。
To the Egyptians, she was known as Hathor.	埃及人稱她為哈索爾。
Another title for her is Giver of Life.	她的另一個稱號是「生命的賜予者」。
Another title for her is The One Who Is All.	她的另一個稱號是「萬物合一者」。
She gave birth to the sun and granted immortality to rulers.	她誕育了太陽，並賜予統治者不朽之身。
The yearly flood of the Nile was caused by the tears she cried.	尼羅河的年年氾濫，據說便是她所流下的眼淚所致。
Her priests and servants were knowns as Pastophori.	她的祭司與侍者被稱為「帕斯托弗里」。
The Romans knew her by the name Aphrodite.	羅馬人稱她為阿芙羅黛蒂。
Mirrors are considered her sacred objects.	鏡子被視為她的聖物。
The Morning Star and Evening Star are named for her.	晨星與昏星，都是以她之名命名。
Her sacred day is Friday on which day her followers would eat fish.	她的聖日是星期五，信徒會在這天食魚。
Her sacred element is copper.	她的聖屬元素是銅。
One of her most important shrines was on the island of Cyprus.	她最重要的聖殿之一，座落於賽普勒斯島。
She was known to the Romans as Hestia.	羅馬人稱她為赫斯提亞。
In the ancient language of Sanscrit, her name means "shining."	在古梵語中，她的名字意為「明亮」。
She is the Guardian of Innermost Things.	她是萬物核心的守護者。
Her sacred fire was tended by six women who took vows of chastity for thirty years.	她的聖火，由六名發願守貞三十年的女子看管。
Her hearth fire is thought to be the center of the earth.	她的爐火，被視為大地的中心。
She is the guardian of home and hearth.	她是家庭與爐灶的守護者。
To the Romans she was known as Mother of the Harvest.	羅馬人稱她為「豐收之母」。
In Greek, her name was Kore or Demeter.	在希臘語中，她被稱為柯瑞或狄蜜特。
She was a guardian of grains and the field.	她是穀物與田野的守護者。
Her major festival was celebrated on April 19th.	她的重大節慶於四月十九日慶祝。
She was renowned as The Lawgiver and her priestesses helped to found the legal system of Rome.	她以「立法者」之名著稱，她的女祭司協助奠定了羅馬的法律體系。
Her sacred women were titled Matronae and ruled Rome for hundreds of years.	她座下的聖女被尊稱為「瑪特羅娜」，統領羅馬達數百年之久。
What is Aphrodite's sacred number?	阿芙羅黛蒂的聖數是什麼？
In the kingdom of flora, what represents fertility and is sacred to Aphrodite?	在花草之界中，什麼象徵生育並為阿芙羅黛蒂所鍾愛？
In the kingdom of fauna, what represents fertility and is sacred to Aphrodite?	在鳥獸之界中，什麼象徵生育並為阿芙羅黛蒂所鍾愛？
To what people was the Goddess well known as Aphrodite?	這位女神以「阿芙羅黛蒂」之名，廣為哪個民族所知？
Whom did Aphrodite love that was killed by a boar?	阿芙羅黛蒂所鍾愛、卻死於野豬之口的人是誰？
Who fell in love with Adonis and refused to release him from the Underworld?	是誰愛上了阿度尼斯，並拒絕將他從冥界放歸？
Who ended the dispute between Aphrodite and Persephone over Adonis?	是誰終結了阿芙羅黛蒂與波瑟芬妮之間，為了阿度尼斯而起的爭執？
Who transformed into a boar and killed Adonis?	是誰化身為野豬，殺死了阿度尼斯？
Where did Pygmalion live?	皮格梅里恩住在何處？
Whom did Pygmalion worship?	皮格梅里恩崇拜的是誰？
Whose company did Pygmalion disdain?	皮格梅里恩不屑與何人為伍？
Of what was the statue made that Pygmalion carved?	皮格梅里恩雕刻的那尊雕像，是用什麼材質製成的？
What did Aphrodite give to the statue to reward Pygmalion?	阿芙羅黛蒂賜給那尊雕像什麼，以獎賞皮格梅里恩？
What is the name of the King who was father to Hippolytus?	希波萊特斯的父王，名叫什麼？
Upon what did Hippolytus ride to go to the hunt?	希波萊特斯前往狩獵時，騎乘的是什麼？
Who did Aphrodite make to fall in love with Hippolytus after he scorned the Goddess?	希波萊特斯輕慢了女神之後，阿芙羅黛蒂讓誰愛上了他？
Upon whom did Theseus call for vengeance upon Hippolytus?	忒修斯向誰祈求，要向希波萊特斯復仇？
Who was dragged to death behind his chariot?	是誰被自己的戰車拖行至死？
