Your bidding, M'Lord:	吾王，請吩咐：
ST. LEONARD'S FOREST\nIt is said that here the holy hermit, St. Leonard, did slay a most fearsome dragon. Where the saint's blood fell upon the ground, lillies-of-the-valley sprouted and flourished in his honor.	聖倫納德森林\n傳說在此地，聖潔的隱士聖倫納德曾斬殺一頭極為凶惡的巨龍。聖徒鮮血灑落之處，鈴蘭遂萌芽茂盛，以紀念此事。
WINDSOR\nThese fertile hunting grounds have long been protected by Cernunnos, Celtic god of the underworld. He has large stag's antlers upon his head and wears a golden torc about his neck.	溫莎\n這片豐饒的獵場，長久以來受凱爾特冥界之神 Cernunnos 所庇護。祂頭上頂著碩大的雄鹿犄角，頸間戴著一只黃金項圈。
